{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-78055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5},\\,s>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-5} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{5t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\ {e}^{5t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-78055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-78055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-78055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t"] ["math" "{e}^{5t}"] ["math" "{t}^{5}"] ["math" "{t}^{5}{e}^{5t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-78055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{5t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{4}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{4}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{u}_{4}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} \\\\ {u}_{4}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} & ={u}_{4}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{u}_{4}(t)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t"] ["math" "{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "{u}_{4}(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{u}_{4}(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4}{3s+6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2}=\\frac{4}{3s+6},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3s+6} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} & =\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t"] ["math" "{t}^{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{3}{2s-4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}=\\frac{3}{2s-4},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2s-4} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-2t}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "{t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{4{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{4{u}_{1}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} \\\\ 4{u}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} & =4{u}_{1}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{u}_{1}(t)"] ["math" "4{e}^{-t}"] ["math" "4{u}_{1}(t)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "{u}_{1}(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{u}_{1}(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}+{e}^{-5s}}{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We decompose the fraction into a sum of fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}+{e}^{-5s}}{s}=\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{8}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-8s}}{s},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{u}_{5}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{5}(t)=u(t-5)$ and ${u}_{8}(t)=u(t-8)$ are the unit step functions.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-8s}}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}} \\\\  & =2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{2{e}^{-8s}+{e}^{-5s}}{s}$ is $f(t)=2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{u}_{8}(t)+{e}^{5t}"] ["math" "2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t)"] ["math" "2{u}_{9}(t)"] ["math" "t{e}^{8t}+{u}_{5}(t)"] ["math" "{u}_{4}(t)+{u}_{5}(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{u}_{8}(t)+{u}_{5}(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{10+3{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10+3{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}}=\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{s}} & =5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}}+3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =5{t}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{10+3{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}}$ is $f(t)=5{t}^{2}+3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-64359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10t+3"] ["math" "10{t}^{2}+3"] ["math" "10{t}^{3}+6t"] ["math" "5t+3"] ["math" "5{t}^{2}+3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5{t}^{2}+3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}+9}-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+9}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}+9}-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}}-5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{6-5s}{{s}^{2}+9}$ is $f(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{8{s}^{3}-24}{{s}^{5}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8{s}^{3}-24}{{s}^{5}}=\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{{t}^{4}} & =\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} & =8{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\  & =8t-{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{8{s}^{3}-24}{{s}^{5}}$ is $f(t)=8t-{t}^{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4-8{t}^{5}"] ["math" "4{t}^{2}-{t}^{5}"] ["math" "8-24{e}^{5t}"] ["math" "8t-{t}^{4}"] ["math" "t-6{t}^{2}{e}^{5t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8t-{t}^{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{2s+15}{{s}^{2}+9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2s+15}{{s}^{2}+9}=\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{15}{{s}^{2}+9}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{15}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}}+5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{2s+15}{{s}^{2}+9}$ is $f(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89816" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89816" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t"] ["math" "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+15\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89816" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${L}^{-1}{\\frac{3s}{4{s}^{2}+16}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t} & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3s}{4{s}^{2}+16}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345614" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345614" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345614" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{8{e}^{-2s}}{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{2}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{2}(t)=u(t-2)$ is the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{2}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{u}_{2}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}} \\\\ {u}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}} & ={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}}=8\\cdot {u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{8{e}^{-2s}}{s}}=8{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-64353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{u}_{8}(t)"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=8{u}_{2}(t)"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{2}{u}_{8}(t)"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{8}{u}_{2}(t)"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={u}_{4}(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=8{u}_{2}(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s-2}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} & ={e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}=4\\cdot {e}^{2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s-2}}=4{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-64348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{4t}"] ["math" "4(t-2)^{2}"] ["math" "4{e}^{2t}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}(t-2)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{2t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{e}^{2t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{3!}{{s}^{3+1}}=\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{t}^{3}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {t}^{3} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} & ={t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}}={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{-\\frac{3}{2{s}^{4}}}=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}"] ["math" "{t}^{3}"] ["math" "{t}^{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2!}{{s}^{2+1}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{t}^{2}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {t}^{2} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}} & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}}={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}}=2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{t}^{2}"] ["math" "2{t}^{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}"] ["math" "{t}^{2}"] ["math" "{t}^{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-4)(s+5)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{(s-4)(s+5)}=\\frac{1}{s-4}-\\frac{1}{s+5}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4 \\\\ L{{e}^{-5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+5},\\,s>-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}-\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\  & ={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-4)(s+5)}$ is $f(t)={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-345623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{5t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=-{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-5t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=4{e}^{t}-5{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{4t}+{e}^{-5t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-345623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{4t}-{e}^{-5t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}$ is $f(t)=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=10{t}^{2}+{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}+3{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}-9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}-9}=\\frac{1}{(s-3)(s+3)}=\\frac{1}{6(s-3)}-\\frac{1}{6(s+3)}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{6(s-3)}-\\frac{1}{6(s+3)}} & =\\frac{1}{6}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}}-\\frac{1}{6}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}-9}$ is $f(t)=\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-{e}^{3t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{9t}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-9t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-3t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}=\\frac{6}{s(s-6)}=\\frac{1}{s-6}-\\frac{1}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{6t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-6},\\,s>6 \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}-\\frac{1}{s}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{6t}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-6s}$ is $f(t)={e}^{6t}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-64381" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64381" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=6{e}^{t}-1"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{-2t}-3"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{-t}-6"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{2t}+6"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{6t}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-64381" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}={e}^{6t}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${L}^{-1}{F(s)}$ for $F(s)=\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+5s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+5s}=\\frac{5}{s(s+5)}=\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s+5}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-5t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+5},\\,s>-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+5s}$ is $f(t)=1-{e}^{-5t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5ae4d10cad4b3211886596f61827eac320b389378b2a8dc67a1aeaa509aa8ccc"} {"question" "q-89826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-5t"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-{e}^{-5t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=t+{t}^{2}{e}^{-5t}"] ["math" "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "q-89826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=1-{e}^{-5t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/state.json" "file_sha256" "89cc710120d31e08796ef2bdebb42ba468eb65187c10e1154e8d8b621654278c"} {"question" "e-6653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\dfrac{3}{s^2 + 9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6653.json" "file_sha256" "9f5b892ee6870bdc63bebcd8043ebd6d2fef97e452c653e70e733a269bfc09cb"} {"question" "e-6653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t} & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+{3}^{2}}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & ={L}^{-1}{L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6653.json" "file_sha256" "9f5b892ee6870bdc63bebcd8043ebd6d2fef97e452c653e70e733a269bfc09cb"} {"question" "e-6655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\}$ for $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6655.json" "file_sha256" "642886ceb7133b8ae825560a48b46bead2572f5a75e9423909cfc25eaa0e97f9"} {"question" "e-6655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s} =\\dfrac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s},\\,s>0, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $u_1(t)=u(t-1)$ is the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}} & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =4{u}_{1}(t)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\} = f(t)= 4 u_1(t) - 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6655.json" "file_sha256" "642886ceb7133b8ae825560a48b46bead2572f5a75e9423909cfc25eaa0e97f9"} {"question" "e-6654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\dfrac{7}{s - 9}\\right\\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6654.json" "file_sha256" "ff6ebc02a37a28775031ac5cf79347892b040d7299bfb6e05c2c49b39f1c09a6"} {"question" "e-6654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{9t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-9},\\,s>9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{9t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-9} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{9t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} \\\\ {e}^{9t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}} & ={e}^{9t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-9}}=7\\cdot {e}^{9t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{7}{s-9}}=7{e}^{9t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6654.json" "file_sha256" "ff6ebc02a37a28775031ac5cf79347892b040d7299bfb6e05c2c49b39f1c09a6"} {"question" "e-6656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6656.json" "file_sha256" "c35fe783b187e3bab6b95506cb28aed00296ba8dd69bad1a4b153b66552c6276"} {"question" "e-6656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)} = \\dfrac{2}{s-4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+2}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4, \\\\ L{{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+2},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s+2}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{ F(s) \\right\\} = f(t)=2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072336/example-6656.json" "file_sha256" "c35fe783b187e3bab6b95506cb28aed00296ba8dd69bad1a4b153b66552c6276"}] "usage" {"q-78055" [] "q-64381" [] "e-6656" [] "e-6653" [] "e-6654" [] "e-6655" []} "basis" 2632 "retractions" [[17592186148149 :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\frac{1}{s - 5}$."] [17592186148098 :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\frac{6}{s^{2} - 6s}$."] [17592186147299 :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s) = \\dfrac{3}{s^2 + 9}$."] [17592186147299 :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{\\sin 3t} &= \\frac{3}{s^{2} + 3^{2}} = \\frac{3}{s^{2} + 9}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{3}{s^{2} + 9}} &= L^{-1}{L{\\sin 3t}} \\\\\n&= \\sin 3t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186147301 :question/problem "Find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\}$ for $F(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}$."] [17592186147301 :question/worked-solution "First, we decompose the fraction into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s} =\\dfrac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{u_{1}(t)} &= \\frac{e^{-s}}{s}, s > 0, \\\\\nL{1} &= \\frac{1}{s}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nu_1(t)=u(t-1)\n$$\n\nis the unit step function.\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{4e^{-s}}{s} - \\frac{2}{s}} &= 4L^{-1}{\\frac{e^{-s}}{s}} - 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\\n&= 4u_{1}(t) - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\dfrac{4e^{-s}-2}{s}\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s)\\right\\} = f(t)= 4 u_1(t) - 2\n$$"] [17592186147300 :question/problem "Compute $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\dfrac{e^{-3s}}{7}\\right\\}$."] [17592186147300 :question/worked-solution "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{δ_{3}(t)} &= e^{-3s}, s > 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\delta_3(t) = \\delta(t-3)\n$$\n\nis the Dirac delta function.\n\nTherefore, using the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{e^{-3s}}{7}} &= \\frac{1}{7}L^{-1}{e^{-3s}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}L^{-1}{L{δ_{3}(t)}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}δ_{3}(t)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186147302 :question/problem "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}$."] [17592186147302 :question/worked-solution "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)} = \\dfrac{2}{s-4} + \\dfrac{1}{s+2}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{e^{4t}} &= \\frac{1}{s - 4}, s > 4, \\\\\nL{e^{-2t}} &= \\frac{1}{s + 2}, s > - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s - 4} + \\frac{1}{s + 2}} &= 2L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s - 4}} + L^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s + 2}} \\\\\n&= 2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\dfrac{3s}{(s-4)(s+2)}\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{F(s) \\right\\} = f(t)=2e^{4t} + e^{-2t}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186146600 17592186146601 17592186146602 17592186146603 17592186146604 17592186146906 17592186146907 17592186146908 17592186146909 17592186146910] "immutable_fields" [[17592186146599 :answer-field/correct] [17592186146599 :answer-field/id] [17592186146599 :answer-field/key] [17592186146599 :answer-field/type] [17592186146905 :answer-field/correct] [17592186146905 :answer-field/id] [17592186146905 :answer-field/key] [17592186146905 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
